  + [authority_scope] is IR7 slice order, gates, expected outputs, model routing, dry-run request boundaries, resource safety boundaries, human approval boundaries, fixture planning boundaries, implementation activation boundary, generated-output boundary, and forbidden live-control scope
  + [implementation_scope] is operations dry-run request simulator planning plus gated implementation activation
  + [depends_on] is docs/planning/Post_IR6_Implementation_Readiness_Surface.v1.sop
  + [depends_on] is docs/reviews/Post_IR6_Implementation_Readiness_Rebake_Review.v1.sop
  + [depends_on] is docs/planning/FSC5_Operations_Safety_Pack.v1.sop
  + [depends_on] is docs/canonical/LangSOP_Operations_Safety_Spec.canonical.sop
  + [depends_on] is docs/planning/IR6_Coordination_Mailbox_Projection_Prototype_Implementation_Proof_Pack.v1.sop
  + [depends_on] is docs/reviews/IR6_Implementation_Completion_Review.v1.sop

  = must: use docs/slices/IR7_Final_Slices.v1.sop as the current IR7 slice surface
  = must: execute IR7-S01 first
  = must: run completion review after each IR7 slice before opening the next gated slice
  = must: keep operation requests, dry-run results, fixture success, human approval displays, coordination claims, mailbox carriers, generated projections, and generated reports non-authoritative
  - never: treat IR7 slices as permission for operations simulator implementation, dependency installation, package metadata mutation, command execution, process control, GPU control, model runtime mutation, job dispatch, credential access or mutation, network exposure mutation, destructive filesystem action, persistent operations automation, operations control, or live machine control

& [CanonicalIR7SliceSet] is the final IR7 slice sequence
  + [slice] is IR7-S01 operations boundary import and invariant reconciliation
  + [slice] is IR7-S02 dry-run operation request, result, refusal, and non-authority contract
  + [slice] is IR7-S03 resource safety, human approval, credential, network, and rollback contract
  + [slice] is IR7-S04 operations dry-run fixture plan and expected ledger plan
  + [slice] is IR7-S05 operations dry-run simulator implementation plan and generated-output boundary
  + [slice] is IR7-S06 IR7 completion review and implementation activation pack

  = must: preserve this order unless completion review rebakes IR7

& [CanonicalIR7ExecutionGate] is the activation rule for IR7
  + [current_ready_slice] is IR7-S01
  + [gated_slice] is IR7-S02 until IR7-S01 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is IR7-S03 until IR7-S02 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is IR7-S04 until IR7-S03 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is IR7-S05 until IR7-S04 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is IR7-S06 until IR7-S05 accepted
  + [completion_gate] is IR7 implementation activation pack accepted after IR7-S06

& [CanonicalIR7ModelRouting] is the model-routing record
  + [IR7-S01] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [IR7-S02] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [IR7-S03] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [IR7-S04] is GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable after IR7-S01 through IR7-S03 acceptance
  + [IR7-S05] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [IR7-S06] is requires deeper reasoning

  = must: keep operation safety semantics, human approval, resource risk, credential and network boundaries, generated-output boundary, and final activation under deeper reasoning
  = must: treat bounded fixture planning as Spark-suitable only after boundary, dry-run, and resource-safety contracts are accepted

